WEBVTT

00:00:01.360 --> 00:00:04.629
In November eighteen sixty-three,
five men left Sydney

00:00:04.629 --> 00:00:06.904
to look for tin on Campbell Island.

00:00:06.904 --> 00:00:08.229
They found none.

00:00:08.229 --> 00:00:10.537
They took a few skins
and turned for home.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.704
On New Year’s Day the Grafton
entered Carnley Harbour.

00:00:18.704 --> 00:00:19.954
Close under the rocks,

00:00:19.954 --> 00:00:22.541
twenty fathoms of line
still found no bottom.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.158
By the second evening one
anchor chain had snapped.

00:00:29.158 --> 00:00:32.203
The other dragged.
At midnight the schooner struck.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:39.174
A quarter of an hour after
the men left the pumps,

00:00:39.174 --> 00:00:41.363
the sea was level with the cabin table.

00:00:45.807 --> 00:00:49.024
In daylight all five
made it onto the stones.

00:00:49.024 --> 00:00:51.549
Thomas Musgrave
and François Raynal came ashore

00:00:51.549 --> 00:00:55.020
with Alick McLaren, Henry Forgés
and George Harris.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:00:59.386
Raynal could scarcely walk.

00:00:59.386 --> 00:01:01.661
From the wreck the men
brought the mainsail.

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:03.509
That night they would sleep under it.

